                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is actually beautifully horrible but what's with the price hike to $24.99? That values this in comparison to squenix games on sale lol. There's been no bugfixes/updates/maintenance and still doesn't run as-is downloaded. You'll likely have to hunt down a mod or try a bunch of workarounds. $5.99 to a $1.99 sale was a fair range before, but now i mean, nothing about this has to be experienced by playing it firsthand, especially in a world where good game supply is oversaturated and the real constraint is time.",
